Processing package: Requirements
Element:136: Covariances stay positive semi-definite and no value becomes non-finite over long runs
Element:137: Authority is enforced per role, per class, and per engagement layer, per the authority matrix
Element:138: Each external party is a configurable endpoint with a message type rather than a bespoke integration
Element:139: The queue orders pending decisions by priority and time remaining, and supports pre-delegation where policy allows
Element:140: No pass criterion or measure target is widened to make a test pass
Element:141: The node exposes a versioned contract for snapshot, event stream, detection submission, and plan decisions
Element:142: The desktop sustains its frame-rate budget with the 3D viewport open under a dense-swarm scenario
Element:143: Every detection carries its source and its receipt time
Element:144: Coverage is computed and coverage gaps are detected and displayed
Element:145: Machine identities authenticate with mutual transport-layer security; operator sessions use short-lived signed tokens
Element:146: Identification evidence names its producer, including model name and version for a machine-learning source
Element:147: Every consequential act is attributable to a person, a role, and a mission time in an audit log
Element:148: Training data and model artefacts live outside this repository; only the manifest enters it
Element:149: Measures are computed from the journal without manual collation
Element:150: The system recommends a cheapest-adequate assignment of resources to tracks within readiness, geometry, and policy
Element:151: Coalition track exchange uses STANAG 4676
Element:152: Default display vocabulary is the agreed standard terms, with a per-deployment override table
Element:153: No verification gate is waived by an agent
Element:154: Schema versions are negotiated explicitly and an incompatible peer is refused, not silently accepted
Element:155: Detection to event-stream publish stays inside its budget on-prem and in cloud
Element:156: The assistant has no tool that changes state and no dependency path to a crate that does
Element:157: The per-frame tick stays inside its budget with ingest, poll, plan, and journal all running
Element:158: Detection to on-screen update stays inside its end-to-end budget in the embedded profile
Element:159: Untrusted text from sensors, peers, annotations, and reports is treated as data by the assistant, never as instruction
Element:160: Deployment profiles differ by configuration and wiring, never by conditional logic in a domain crate
Element:161: Observations from heterogeneous sensors are ingested through one governed gateway that validates and quarantines
Element:162: No `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside tests, entry points, and debug-only invariant checks
Element:163: Every artefact is unclassified and derived from public sources
Element:164: No dependency edge exists that `ARCHITECTURE.md` does not draw
Element:165: Every release carries a bill of materials, a signature, and its assurance reports
Element:166: Data is encrypted in transit on every network crossing and at rest where the deployment requires it
Element:167: Detections are exportable in a columnar format for analytics and bulk exchange
Element:168: Sensor modes, tasking, and calibration are held in a registry and changeable by the sensor manager
Element:169: Data from sources with different clocks is time-disciplined and skew is detected
Element:170: Classification and identification produce evidence with a margin rule and per-class thresholds set by policy
Element:171: Every layout carries a status strip stating what the system knows and does not know
Element:172: The node journal fsyncs every envelope; desktop journals fsync on session save and every five seconds
Element:173: Every dependency is recorded in the standards document §2.9 and pinned once
Element:174: Envelopes carry a bus sequence number and a mission time
Element:175: Every recommendation carries a rationale and its alternatives
Element:176: A desktop falls back to embedded operation within its budget after link loss, stores and forwards to capacity, and reconciles within its budget
Element:177: Tracks carry a quality and a staleness that the interface renders differently from fresh data
Element:178: Cooperative identity from open protocols is decoded and fused as evidence
Element:179: Views, reports, and the interface contract carry a releasability marking
Element:180: Absence, staleness, and degradation are visible rather than inferred from silence
Element:181: The graphics and compute contexts stay separate and separately pinned
Element:182: An accepted envelope is durable within its budget, and the node recovers to serving within its budget after restart
Element:183: The two binaries contain wiring, not domain logic
Element:184: Radar feeds decode from ASTERIX category 048
Element:185: A multi-sensor, multi-rate, out-of-sequence tracking pipeline maintains the picture
Element:186: Journals merge in mission-time order, duplicates are dropped, and conflicting decisions are reported rather than resolved
Element:187: Each role has a workspace containing what that role's threads need and not more
Element:188: No engagement, effector command, or reserved identity declaration executes without a recorded human decision
Element:189: A session is journaled, replayable, and reproduces the same picture
Element:190: Snapshot calls do not touch the pipeline and stay inside their budget
Element:191: Pending decisions escalate and time out rather than waiting indefinitely
Element:192: Machine assistance is labelled, sourced, and carries no authority in the interface
Element:193: The node sustains its detection ingest throughput through validation and quarantine
Element:194: Weapons control status is set by the authorized roles and constrains every recommendation
Element:195: Entities keep a global identity with lineage across sources and sessions
Element:196: Threats are scored against a defended-asset list with per-class lethality and asset weighting
Element:197: Every source is authenticated before its data enters the picture
Element:198: Unimplemented capability returns a named error on every reachable path
Element:199: Shared types have exactly one owning crate; everything above re-exports
